            <ArticleTitle>Risk for subsequent coronary artery disease after preeclampsia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>805-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We studied the history of hypertensive pregnancies and conventional risk factors in 141 relatively young (&lt;66 years) parous women with angiographically documented coronary artery disease and in age-matched controls. Our study showed that hypertension, diabetes, hypercholesterolemia, advanced age, smoking, and preeclampsia are independent risk factors for subsequent coronary artery disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
